WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.815
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.115 --> 00:00:10.081
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.381 --> 00:00:17.829
Unit two: Past Simple and Past Continuous. Today you will talk about finished events and actions in progress in the past.

4
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:20.688
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:25.029
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.966
Yesterday.

7
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.368
Yesterday means the day before today.

8
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:32.890
I visited my aunt yesterday.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:35.950
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.859
Yesterday.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.606
Last week.

12
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:44.721
Last week means the week before this one.

13
00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:46.631
We met last week.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.706
Your turn. Say: Last week.

15
00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.835
Last week.

16
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.364
Ago.

17
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.966
Ago means before now.

18
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.132
He left two hours ago.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:03.381
Your turn. Say: Ago.

20
00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:07.083
Ago.

21
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.130
Regular verb.

22
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:13.417
Regular verb means a verb that adds -ed in the past.

23
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:15.656
Walk is a regular verb.

24
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.204
Your turn. Say: Regular verb.

25
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.277
Regular verb.

26
00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.273
Irregular verb.

27
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.490
Irregular verb means a verb with a special past form.

28
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:31.293
Go becomes went.

29
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:35.128
Your turn. Say: Irregular verb.

30
00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:39.618
Irregular verb.

31
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:41.280
While.

32
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:44.086
While means during the time that.

33
00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:46.544
I was reading while she was cooking.

34
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:49.640
Your turn. Say: While.

35
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.640
While.

36
00:01:54.383 --> 00:01:55.083
When.

37
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:57.723
When means at the time that.

38
00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.956
I was sleeping when you called.

39
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.529
Your turn. Say: When.

40
00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.066
When.

41
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:07.771
Interrupt.

42
00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:11.073
Interrupt means to stop an action.

43
00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:13.358
The rain interrupted the game.

44
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.463
Your turn. Say: Interrupt.

45
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.185
Interrupt.

46
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.953
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:28.559
Visal, how do we form the past simple?

48
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:44.472
We add -ed to regular verbs, such as walked and played. Irregular verbs change, for example go becomes went and see becomes saw. In questions and negatives we use did and the base verb.

49
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:47.513
What is the past continuous?

50
00:02:48.617 --> 00:02:58.479
It is was or were plus the -ing form. We use it for an action in progress at a past time, such as At eight o'clock I was studying.

51
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:01.095
How do we use them together?

52
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:12.020
We use the past continuous for a longer action and the past simple for a shorter action that interrupted it: I was cooking when the lights went out.

53
00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.864
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:21.629
Grammar focus: Past simple: V-ed; past continuous: was and were plus V-ing.

55
00:03:21.929 --> 00:03:23.139
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.140
I visited my aunt yesterday.

57
00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.957
I was cooking when the lights went out.

58
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:38.105
Finished past events use the past simple. Actions in progress use was or were plus verb-ing. A short action can interrupt a long one.

59
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:42.559
Be careful! Don't say: I go to the market yesterday.

60
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.685
Say: I went to the market yesterday.

61
00:03:46.985 --> 00:03:48.451
Use the past form.

62
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.815
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.938
A Rainy Evening.

64
00:03:54.238 --> 00:03:56.504
Last night Dara was doing his homework.

65
00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.244
Suddenly the lights went out.

66
00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:03.022
His mother brought a candle while he was looking for his book.

67
00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.904
They talked quietly until the electricity came back.

68
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.248
Then he finished his work and went to bed.

69
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:15.463
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.317 --> 00:04:18.223
I blank to the market yesterday.

71
00:04:18.523 --> 00:04:21.712
A, go. B, was going. C, went.

72
00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.895
The answer is C: went.

73
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.922
She was reading when the phone blank.

74
00:04:30.222 --> 00:04:33.771
A, rang. B, was ringing. C, rings.

75
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:38.973
The answer is A: rang.

76
00:04:40.117 --> 00:04:41.710
Which is an irregular verb?

77
00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.932
A, play. B, see. C, walk.

78
00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.188
The answer is B: see.

79
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.675
What was Dara doing when the lights went out?

80
00:04:53.975 --> 00:04:57.593
A, cooking. B, sleeping. C, his homework.

81
00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.005
The answer is C: his homework.

82
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.289
Which word means 'during the time that'?

83
00:05:06.589 --> 00:05:09.859
A, while. B, ago. C, last.

84
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.063
The answer is A: while.

85
00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:19.441
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.283 --> 00:05:22.132
Tell me what you did last weekend.

87
00:05:30.917 --> 00:05:32.382
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.682 --> 00:05:43.441
Last weekend I visited my grandmother in the village. We cooked fish soup together, and I was helping her when my cousin arrived. In the evening we played games until it was dark.

89
00:05:43.741 --> 00:05:45.810
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:46.717 --> 00:05:54.326
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple: v-ed; past continuous: was and were plus v-ing.

91
00:05:54.626 --> 00:05:58.579
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

92
00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:01.276
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:06:01.576 --> 00:06:04.786
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

